-- title:
--   Unramifiedness at vertical height-one primes over the floor, q=3
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$, containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ for which some ring embedding $L\to\mathbb{C}$ sends $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((t))$ obtained as `laurentBaseChange`, i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field `xHFunctionField` of level $q^2M'$ for the subgroup $H\le(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ that is the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, with maximal ideal generated by $\varpi$, and with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A\to L\to K$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) under coefficient extension, and let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ consisting exactly of those $f$ admitting power series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ nonzero modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ and $f\cdot y = x$ after mapping coefficients to $L$. Let $z$ be a point of the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak{X}=$ `TwoChartIntegralModel` $A$ $K$ $j$ (the pushout of the two chart spectra), let $\varpi_z$ be the germ at $z$ of the global section pulled back from $\varpi$ along $\mathfrak{X}\to\operatorname{Spec}A$, and assume $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk at $z$. Let $y$ be a point of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j$-finite chart algebra `chartAlgFin` $A$ $K$ $j$ (the elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$) mapping to $z$, with $y$ maximal; let $\Omega$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ and $\varphi$ a ring homomorphism from the chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, such that $\varphi(j)$ is not in `ssJSet` $q$ $\Omega$, the set of $j$-values all of whose elliptic curves over $\Omega$ have trivial $q$-torsion. Assume every element of the chart algebra lying in the nonunits of $W_0$ belongs to $y$. Finally let $K_0$ be the $L$-base change of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_0(M')$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, with $K_0\le K$ and compatible $A$-algebra structure, let $j_0\in K_0$ be nonzero with the same Laurent expansion, and let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from `chartAlgFin` $A$ $K_0$ $j_0$ to `chartAlgFin` $A$ $K$ $j$ inducing the inclusion $K_0\hookrightarrow K$. Then, for the algebra structure given by $\iota$, every prime ideal $\mathfrak{Q}$ of `chartAlgFin` $A$ $K$ $j$ with $\mathfrak{Q}\subseteq y$, of height one, and containing the image of $\varpi$, satisfies `Algebra.IsUnramifiedAt` over `chartAlgFin` $A$ $K_0$ $j_0$.
--
--   This is the unramifiedness statement for the integral model of the full-level-$q$ modular curve over the integral model of $X_0(M')$, at vertical (characteristic-$q$) height-one primes through a closed point of the special fibre that has ordinary $j$-invariant and lies on the branch cut out by the Gauss valuation ring $W_0$, in the case $q=3$. It feeds the proof that the local ring of the fibre at such a maximal ideal is regular, and thence the semistability and level-lowering input of the Frey-curve argument.
-- source:
